{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T21:56:07.823Z","ordinal":35936,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b02137009cc87d29932b646907008d6","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6edc2fb6d810450dbf01524e9a4091d9","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"body_file=$(mktemp)\\ncat > \\\"$body_file\\\" <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Add real `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` coverage for model-generated attempts to add `authorizedScope`, `permittedCapabilities`, `executionMode`, and child-limit fields to `spawn_subagent`.\\n- Assert the model-facing schema does not offer authority grants and the malformed request is rejected before child construction or inference.\\n- Add runtime compatibility coverage for prompt-only delegation, independent child context, and bounded result return.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `node --import tsx --test test/subagent_delegation_authority.test.ts` — 4/4 passed under Node 24 with isolated `HOME` and XDG paths.\\n- `npm exec tsc -- --noEmit` — passed.\\n- Full suite is delegated to hosted CI per the user's instruction to rely on hosted checks.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- XERJ definition-first lookup found the existing `runSubagent` path (`cli/src/agent.ts:4609`), host role allowlists (`cli/src/core/roles.ts`), and the dispatcher enforcement point (`cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts`).\\n- Reused Nexus's local `AutonomousAgent`, deterministic OpenAI-compatible gateway fixture, and leak guard. The end-to-end boundary test exercises schema generation, handler validation, and the actual parent/child request flow together. No peer implementation was copied.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nTest-only. No provider or gateway changes.\\nEOF\\ngh pr create --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --base main --head v1/pa4-transient-contract-tests --title \\\"test(delegation): exercise transient contract boundaries\\\" --body-file \\\"$body_file\\\"\\nrm -f \\\"$body_file\\\"\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/pa4-transient-contract-tests\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:600}); text(JSON.stringify(r))\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20014-b98e-7f50-9b44-1c38f2a1201a","create_time":1795298160.0400662}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16037,"sampled_through_sequence":16034,"client_authored":false}}
