{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:35:05.630Z","ordinal":36580,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-927d67bc-9114-42f0-885d-e18902f9b464","process_id":"51056","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"PA4|WP-P10-02|delegat|/loop|/goal|/batch\" docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md docs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md docs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md | head -n 180"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'PA4|WP-P10-02|delegat|/loop|/goal|/batch' docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md docs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md docs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","query":"PA4|WP-P10-02|delegat|/loop|/goal|/batch","path":"PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:41:**Design / reuse:** Extend `ContinuationBudget` and existing durable objective/operation records with a task budget id, maximum total steps/tool invocations/inference submissions/elapsed time/tokens, per-tool deadline and delegation depth. Persist consumed counters before/after side effects with `withDurableSync`. Child agents inherit the parent’s remaining budget; provider retry consumes the same inference allowance. A resumed task cannot regain budget. Require explicit operator-authorized budget renewal after exhaustion.\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:79:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:108:2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:1:# PA-4 transient delegation authority milestone\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:12:- Active children, delegated inference steps, and execution duration are bounded. Defaults are four active children, 64 delegated inference requests per parent turn, and two minutes per child.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:17:These restrictions preserve prompt-only compatibility while intentionally refusing legacy prompt-only requests that relied on unrestricted writes. The process-wide active-child ceiling is shared by transient delegations; aggregate budgets across separate parent agents and independent evidence review remain open PA-4 work.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:1:# PA-4 baseline: delegation and workflow execution\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:7:| Interactive turns and inference | Implemented | `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` delegates to `runTurnImpl` ([agent.ts:4186](../../cli/src/agent.ts#L4186), [run_turn.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/run_turn.ts#L26)); provider recovery and context admission are in the turn path. `TurnResult` distinguishes interrupted, blocked and failed executions and requires evidence for verified outcomes ([turn.ts:17](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L17), [turn.ts:423](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L423)). |\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:8:| Transient delegation | Partially implemented; qualification pending | `runSubagent` remains the in-turn child path ([agent.ts](../../cli/src/agent.ts)); `spawn_subagent` now selects a predefined profile, narrows tools at schema and dispatcher boundaries, clears inherited full access, and emits a typed receipt ([spine_handlers.ts](../../cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts), [dispatch_tool_call.ts](../../cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts)). Prompt-only calls default to read-only `semantic_explorer`; writable profiles require an established worktree. Depth and per-parent child-attempt limits are enforced. Process-wide resource budgets, full task/session/workspace grant derivation, deterministic security tests, and independent evidence review remain outstanding; see [transient authority milestone](PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md).\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:13:| `/loop`, `/goal`, `/batch` | `/batch` implemented, `/loop` and `/goal` unimplemented | `/batch` is present in the command catalogue and routes to `BatchOrchestrator`; it validates existing operation JSON specs and persists through `OperationStore` and `OperationRunner` ([batch.ts](../../cli/src/batch.ts), [batch_spec.ts](../../cli/src/batch_spec.ts), [router.ts](../../cli/src/slash/router.ts), [repl.ts](../../cli/src/repl.ts)). `batch.test.ts` and `batch_spec.test.ts` cover command behavior. `/loop` and `/goal` lifecycle controllers remain absent; loop detector tests do not implement durable loop state, and the objective ledger has no `/goal` lifecycle.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:14:| Pause, cancellation and restart | Implemented, incomplete | Durable operations include distinct `PAUSED`, cancellation and bounded restart reconciliation ([operation.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts), [operation_runner.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts), [operation_cli.ts](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts)). `/batch` pause is honored at a safe boundary. Unknown effects still need stronger reconciliation semantics for the broader delegation assignment; `/loop` lifecycle recovery is absent.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:19:- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:26:- `/batch` uses operation specifications and the existing `OperationStore`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, and `OperationRunner`; it defaults to sequential execution. Parallel admission requires isolated worktrees and, as of PA-1 resource-admission work, explicit per-operation CPU/memory reservations. This adds no second scheduler or persisted workflow store.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:27:- `/batch` is wired into the sidecar slash router and REPL, so the TUI obtains its completion/help entry from the same slash catalogue. The implemented actions are `run`, `validate`, `status`, `list`, `pause`, `resume`, `cancel`, and `results`. Pause writes the durable `PAUSED` status at a safe boundary. `/loop` and `/goal` lifecycles remain unimplemented.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:28:- Regression tests cover quoting/Unicode, workspace and symlink boundaries, sequential execution, durable state, partial aggregation, CPU/memory admission and legacy serial fallback. The PA-1 slice passed 44 focused operation/batch tests, 28 operation release/review tests, and the CLI TypeScript build in its isolated worktree. These are targeted results; they do not replace the prescribed full-suite qualification. No provider code changed.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:29:- A definition-first XERJ lookup in the `opencode` corpus found `packages/schema/src/goal.ts:11` (MIT) with bounded round count, stall count, and boot identity fields. This informed the roadmap comparison only; no peer code was copied. The corpus is flagged as incompletely indexed, and the listed `goose` corpus was unavailable.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:30:- This is an implementation checkpoint, not completion evidence for PA-4. Authority enforcement, prompt-only runtime compatibility tests, distinct pause semantics, `/loop`, `/goal`, full batch terminal-state persistence, adversarial coverage, interface-level behavior tests, minimal-provider workflow fixtures, independent review, and comparative evaluation remain outstanding.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:19:- **Peers, read from source** (shallow clones of 2026-11-13/14; Codex at commit 336b19a; untrusted code, nothing run): ACP servers in goose (`crates/goose/src/acp`), Cline (`apps/cli/src/acp/acpAgent.ts`), Gemini CLI (`packages/cli/src/acp`) and opencode (`packages/cli/src/acp/agent.ts`), the Codex `app-server` (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, websocket or UDS; schema generated from Rust types and checked in); schedulers in goose (`scheduler/full.rs`), Cline (`*.cron.md` and event specs) and opencode (a `ScheduleTable` with `in`/`at`/`every`/`cron` and an optional deterministic wake `check`); hooks in Gemini CLI (`docs/hooks/reference.md`), goose (`hooks/mod.rs`), Cline and Codex; extension manifests in Gemini CLI (`gemini-extension.json`), goose (Open Plugins and Gemini formats) and opencode; policy tiers in Gemini CLI (`core/src/policy/config.ts:67-71`), opencode (`managed-policy.ts`) and Codex (`requirements.toml`); goal state in opencode (`schema/src/goal.ts`) and Codex (`thread/goal/*`).\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:21:- **Research notes** (2026-11-15): the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report (read in full; a vendor document with no methodology, customer-reported figures) and OpenHands (documentation, not source) support three priorities here: VR-1 and VR-2 (the report's own evidence is that people delegate what is cheaply checkable, so verifiability is the delegation boundary), PA-1 (it names a view of concurrent agent sessions) and AC-1 (above). They are framing, not evidence about Nexus.\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:97:| PA-4 | **Bounded delegation and workflow commands** (trail 428; [baseline](PA4_BASELINE.md)): extend transient `spawn_subagent` and durable operations with a shared validated delegation contract/outcome, enforce authority intersection and recursive/resource limits, then expose real `/goal`, `/loop`, and `/batch` lifecycles through REPL and TUI/sidecar. Reuse `TeamOrchestrator`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, `OperationStore`, `ResourceRegistry`, specialist profiles, provider recovery, completion evidence, and existing stagnation detectors; do not add a second scheduler or workflow store. `/goal` owns an immutable objective and requirement/evidence ledger; `/loop` is bounded and verifier-driven; `/batch` validates a task graph and maps it into existing work units. Parsing, cancellation, pause/resume, status, recovery, and provider-neutral fixtures are part of each command contract. Spec-format validation may proceed independently; lifecycle and shared-contract work depends on PA-1/PA-2 evidence and WP-P10-02, with `/goal` semantics aligned to PA-3. | prompt-only subagent compatibility; parent/profile/session authority intersection and enforced recursive limits; typed non-success and unknown-effect outcomes; each command has durable state, lifecycle controls, recovery and status through supported interfaces; dependency and workspace conflicts cannot silently complete or overwrite; deterministic verifiers and independent review gate acceptance; standard-contract mock plus existing local/cloud fixtures pass without provider changes | L (staged packages) | P1 |\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:105:PA-4 is staged: the existing operation-spec validator can be reused independently; command lifecycles and shared delegation changes follow WP-P10-02 and verified PA-1/PA-2 gates. `/goal` must also satisfy PA-3 before promotion.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":39420}},"started_at_ms":1795300505629,"completed_at_ms":1795300505629}}
