9Z\\\",\\\"pid\\\":2659835}\\n.git/nexus-claims/SUITE.released-20261031T1045Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"codex-root\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"mike-dev\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/rc15-durable-operation-journal\\\",\\\"worktree\\\":\\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc15-durable-operation-journal\\\",\\\"base\\\":\\\"2e402ca13ab3bdc012f780240a32aaeb3ef010bf\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-10-31T10:08:30Z\\\",\\\"pid\\\":3109880,\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Focused regression only: harness.test.ts worktree durable operation journal identity. No inference or full suite.\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_harness.test_ts.released-20261105T142659Z/owner.json\\n{\\n  \\\"agent\\\": \\\"/root\\\",\\n  \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\",\\n  \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/rc14-node24-run-tests-flake-20261030\\\",\\n  \\\"base\\\": \\\"3e37f78028d470facd59ce675e4fc98523794cf4\\\",\\n  \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-30T13:02:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": \\\"Diagnose exact-main/PR346 Node24-only failure in RustCoreBridge run_tests test; permitted file cli/test/harness.test.ts only; targeted isolated tests only; no product source edits, gateway, or held-out data\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"Candidate merged current origin/main without rewriting history; PR diff remains only the previously accepted 12-insertion/2-deletion test fixture correction. Waiting for fresh main CI and E2 suite ownership release before focused rerun/push.\\\",\\n  \\\"head\\\": \\\"57f45ac1a150ce86a8e62edc2ea7416372077ae9\\\",\\n  \\\"review\\\": \\\"ACCEPT by review_rc14_e5_evidence on exact test diff; no edits\\\",\\n  \\\"reviewed_at\\\": \\\"2026-10-30T13:09:00Z\\\",\\n  \\\"validation\\\": \\\"Focused isolated Node22.22.2 and Node24.21.0 runs PASS; diff-check PASS; no full-suite overlap.\\\"\\n}\\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_RECOVERED_OPERATION_VERIFICATION_20261029.released-20261105T142659Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"codex-root-recovery-fix\\\",\\\"host\\\":\\\"mike-dev\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/recovered-operation-verification-20261029\\\",\\\"worktree\\\":\\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/recovered-operation-verification-20261029\\\",\\\"base\\\":\\\"0f9da7ce040a26bb3df60b43101665f949fb36a0\\\",\\\"head\\\":\\\"97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-10-29T00:28:00Z\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"PR311 P1: merged execution without durable result must remain EXECUTION_UNKNOWN/blocked; require explicit restart from merged source and verification; preserve durable receipt assertions.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"PR #313 independent ACCEPT recorded in PR comment 6485283214 on exact head 97ad3f411a6343ef34fad31f65ad2462c8bc17e5; Node22/24 PASS; Linux CI still running npm test; awaiting exact-head Linux completion before integration into PR #311 branch.\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_repl.ts.released-20261110T063338Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"wp1306-a1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/v114-provider-wait-resume\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-11-10T06:32:58Z\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_agent.ts.released-20261110T064147Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"tui-d03-d04\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/v114-wp1317-d04\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_flight.ts.released-20261110T075447Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"wp1306-a1\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/v114-provider-wait-resume\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-11-10T07:53:54Z\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/DEFECT_HTML_CONTROL_INJECTION_20261023.released-20261105T142659Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex-root\\\", \\\"host\\\": \\\"mike-dev\\\", \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/defect-html-control-injection\\\", \\\"worktree\\\": \\\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/html-control-injection\\\", \\\"base\\\": \\\"4bf6e2b041dc2efb54af551a73796aacc54494a3\\\", \\\"head\\\": \\\"7f202f7a18d15ab35a2a3d36ecc1670c6c0e486b\\\", \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-10-23T23:31:00Z\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"fix terminal carriage-return spoofing in HTML decoded text and search URL fields; refresh PR #175 to current main; add regressions and obtain independent review; no held-out access\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_agent.ts.released-20261119-rd7/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\": \\\"codex-root\\\", \\\"branch\\\": \\\"v1/p10-wp-p10-02-durable-budget\\\", \\\"since\\\": \\\"2026-11-19T06:35:52.974965+00:00\\\", \\\"pid\\\": 1257166, \\\"scope\\\": \\\"WP-P10-02 durable task-level budgets\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_team_convergence.test.ts/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"codex\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/pa4-transient-authority\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-11-21T10:00:00Z\\\",\\\"pid\\\":2290389,\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Update delegation compatibility fixtures for PA-4\\\"}\\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_agent.ts.released-20261110T032707Z/owner.json\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"tui-d03-d04\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/v114-wp1317-d04\\\"}\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"d598f0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.476512252,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":376,\"output\":\"## v1/pa4-orchestration...origin/main [ahead 2, behind 164]\\n?? .gemini/\\nf0b61e05 (HEAD -> v1/pa4-orchestration) feat(delegation): add validated contract and outcomes\\n1223107b feat(batch): validate batch specs on operation schema\\nf873787a test(lsp): exercise navigation across three-file projects (#640)\\nd3a42a07 fix(mcp): avoid replaying ambiguous tool calls (#641)\\nd4cb8be8 Merge pull request #638 from mikeholownych/v1/v1.2x-claude-auth-reconcile\\n421170e5 fix(operations): record checkpoint restores in journal\\n72e22880 fix(auth): serialize rotating sign-in refreshes\\n7d095a21 fix(reliability): sync private stores and recover stale upgrade locks\\n cli/src/batch_spec.ts                |  30 +++++\\n cli/src/core/delegation_contract.ts  | 228 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n cli/test/batch_spec.test.ts          |  42 +++++++\\n cli/test/delegation_contract.test.ts | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++\\n docs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md          |  22 ++++\\n docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md                  |   2 +\\n 6 files changed, 458 insertions(+)\\n[{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"v1/v122-stable\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"ce2c951e249d581e97dd19bcf1d771de62eb5157\\\",\\\"number\\\":686,\\\"title\\\":\\\"chore(release): v1.2.2\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/686\\\"},{\\\"baseRefName\\\":\\\"main\\\",\\\"headRefName\\\":\\\"v1/v122-rc1-g114-evidence\\\",\\\"headRefOid\\\":\\\"c9e6be0151d85f897d91a6f18193c62ad707f04c\\\",\\\"number\\\":685,\\\"title\\\":\\\"docs(evidence): G1.1-4 on the v1.2.2-rc.1 archive\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/685\\\"}]\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3f2d88\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00003942,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2495,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2495)\\nTotal output lines: 22\\n\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:33:## WP-P10-02 — Durable task-level execution budgets\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:41:**Design / reuse:** Extend `ContinuationBudget` and existing durable objective/operation records with a task budget id, maximum total steps/tool invocations/inference submissions/elapsed time/tokens, per-tool deadline and delegation depth. Persist consumed counters before/after side effects with `withDurableSync`. Child agents inherit the parent’s remaining budget; provider retry consumes the same inference allowance. A resumed task cannot regain budget. Require explicit operator-authorized budget renewal after exhaustion.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:79:**Priority:** P1 · **Complexity:** M/L · **Dependencies:** WP-P10-02.\\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:108:2. **WP-P10-02** aggregate budgets across direct, delegated, retry and resume paths (P0).\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:1:# PA-4 transient delegation authority milestone\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:12:- Active children, delegated inference steps, and execution duration are bounded. Defaults are four active children, 64 delegated inference requests per parent turn, and two minutes per child.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md:17:These restrictions preserve prompt-only compatibility while intentionally refusing legacy prompt-only requests that relied on unrestricted writes. The process-wide active-child ceiling is shared by transient delegations; aggregate budgets across separate parent agents and independent evidence review remain open PA-4 work.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:1:# PA-4 baseline: delegation and workflow execution\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:7:| Interactive turns and inference | Implemented | `AutonomousAgent.runTurn` delegates to `runTurnImpl` ([agent.ts:4186](../../cli/src/agent.ts#L4186), [run_turn.ts:26](../../cli/src/core/run_turn.ts#L26)); provider recovery and context admission are in the turn path. `TurnResult` distinguishes interrupted, blocked and failed executions and requires evidence for verified outcomes ([turn.ts:17](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L17), [turn.ts:423](../../cli/src/core/turn.ts#L423)). |\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:8:| Transient delegation | Partially implemented; qualification pending | `runSubagent` remains the in-turn child path ([agent.ts](../../cli/src/agent.ts)); `spawn_subagent` now selects a predefined profile, narrows tools at schema and dispatcher boundaries, clears inherited full access, and emits a typed receipt ([spine_handlers.ts](../../cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts), [dispatch_tool_call.ts](../../cli/src/core/dispatch_tool_call.ts)). Prompt-only calls default to read-only `semantic_explorer`; writable profiles require an established worktree. Depth and per-parent child-attempt limits are enforced. Process-wide resource budgets, full task/session/workspace grant derivation, deterministic security tests, and independent evidence review remain outstanding; see [transient authority milestone](PA4_TRANSIENT_AUTHORITY.md).\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:13:| `/loop`, `/goal`, `/batch` | `/batch` implemented, `/loop` and `/goal` unimplemented | `/batch` is present in the command catalogue and routes to `BatchOrchestrator`; it validates existing operation JSON specs and persists through `OperationStore` and `OperationRunner` ([batch.ts](../../cli/src/batch.ts), [batch_spec.ts](../../cli/src/batch_spec.ts), [router.ts](../../cli/src/slash/router.ts), [repl.ts](../../cli/src/repl.ts)). `batch.test.ts` and `batch_spec.test.ts` cover command behavior. `/loop` and `/goal` lifecycle controllers remain absent; loop detector tests do not implement durable loop state, and the objective ledger has no `/goal` lifecycle.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:14:| Pause, cancellation and restart | Implemented, incomplete | Durable operations include distinct `PAUSED`, cancellation and bounded restart reconciliation ([operation.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation.ts), [operation_runner.ts](../../cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts), [operation_cli.ts](../../cli/src/operation_cli.ts)). `/batch` pause is honored at a safe boundary. Unknown effects still need stronger reconciliation semantics for the broader delegation assignment; `/loop` lifecycle recovery is absent.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:19:- v1.3 PA-1, PA-2 and PA-3 already cover parallel visibility, verified integration and goal semantics. PA-4 stages this assignment against those units and the active WP-P10-02 durable-budget work.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:26:- …195 tokens truncated…egression tests cover quoting/Unicode, workspace and symlink boundaries, sequential execution, durable state, partial aggregation, CPU/memory admission and legacy serial fallback. The PA-1 slice passed 44 focused operation/batch tests, 28 operation release/review tests, and the CLI TypeScript build in its isolated worktree. These are targeted results; they do not replace the prescribed full-suite qualification. No provider code changed.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:29:- A definition-first XERJ lookup in the `opencode` corpus found `packages/schema/src/goal.ts:11` (MIT) with bounded round count, stall count, and boot identity fields. This informed the roadmap comparison only; no peer code was copied. The corpus is flagged as incompletely indexed, and the listed `goose` corpus was unavailable.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PA4_BASELINE.md:30:- This is an implementation checkpoint, not completion evidence for PA-4. Authority enforcement, prompt-only runtime compatibility tests, distinct pause semantics, `/loop`, `/goal`, full batch terminal-state persistence, adversarial coverage, interface-level behavior tests, minimal-provider workflow fixtures, independent review, and comparative evaluation remain outstanding.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:19:- **Peers, read from source** (shallow clones of 2026-11-13/14; Codex at commit 336b19a; untrusted code, nothing run): ACP servers in goose (`crates/goose/src/acp`), Cline (`apps/cli/src/acp/acpAgent.ts`), Gemini CLI (`packages/cli/src/acp`) and opencode (`packages/cli/src/acp/agent.ts`), the Codex `app-server` (JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, websocket or UDS; schema generated from Rust types and checked in); schedulers in goose (`scheduler/full.rs`), Cline (`*.cron.md` and event specs) and opencode (a `ScheduleTable` with `in`/`at`/`every`/`cron` and an optional deterministic wake `check`); hooks in Gemini CLI (`docs/hooks/reference.md`), goose (`hooks/mod.rs`), Cline and Codex; extension manifests in Gemini CLI (`gemini-extension.json`), goose (Open Plugins and Gemini formats) and opencode; policy tiers in Gemini CLI (`core/src/policy/config.ts:67-71`), opencode (`managed-policy.ts`) and Codex (`requirements.toml`); goal state in opencode (`schema/src/goal.ts`) and Codex (`thread/goal/*`).\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:21:- **Research notes** (2026-11-15): the Anthropic 2026 agentic coding trends report (read in full; a vendor document with no methodology, customer-reported figures) and OpenHands (documentation, not source) support three priorities here: VR-1 and VR-2 (the report's own evidence is that people delegate what is cheaply checkable, so verifiability is the delegation boundary), PA-1 (it names a view of concurrent agent sessions) and AC-1 (above). They are framing, not evidence about Nexus.\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:97:| PA-4 | **Bounded delegation and workflow commands** (trail 428; [baseline](PA4_BASELINE.md)): extend transient `spawn_subagent` and durable operations with a shared validated delegation contract/outcome, enforce authority intersection and recursive/resource limits, then expose real `/goal`, `/loop`, and `/batch` lifecycles through REPL and TUI/sidecar. Reuse `TeamOrchestrator`, `ConvergenceScheduler`, `OperationStore`, `ResourceRegistry`, specialist profiles, provider recovery, completion evidence, and existing stagnation detectors; do not add a second scheduler or workflow store. `/goal` owns an immutable objective and requirement/evidence ledger; `/loop` is bounded and verifier-driven; `/batch` validates a task graph and maps it into existing work units. Parsing, cancellation, pause/resume, status, recovery, and provider-neutral fixtures are part of each command contract. Spec-format validation may proceed independently; lifecycle and shared-contract work depends on PA-1/PA-2 evidence and WP-P10-02, with `/goal` semantics aligned to PA-3. | prompt-only subagent compatibility; parent/profile/session authority intersection and enforced recursive limits; typed non-success and unknown-effect outcomes; each command has durable state, lifecycle controls, recovery and status through supported interfaces; dependency and workspace conflicts cannot silently complete or overwrite; deterministic verifiers and independent review gate acceptance; standard-contract mock plus existing local/cloud fixtures pass without provider changes | L (staged packages) | P1 |\\ndocs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:105:PA-4 is staged: the existing operation-spec validator can be reused independently; command lifecycles and shared delegation changes follow WP-P10-02 and verified PA-1/PA-2 gates. `/goal` must also satisfy PA-3 before promotion.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"65deb6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.233213072,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":636,\"output\":\"# Reference coding with XERJ\\n\\nThe detail behind the \\\"Reference coding\\\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\\n\\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \\\"Reference coding\\\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \\\"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\\\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \\\"<words>\\\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \\\"<words>\\\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \\\"<symbol>\\\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \\\"<model>\\\" --used-for \\\"<task>\\\" --verdict \\\"<what worked and what did not>\\\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\\na5fa1dca54c176e50f16176fe82454a2dff360e6\\trefs/heads/main\\n{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"jobs\\\":[{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"cloudflare-experiment (24)\\\",\\\"running\\\":[],\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (24)\\\",\\\"running\\\":[\\\"Run the CLI suite with a hang bound\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test-matrix (22)\\\",\\\"running\\\":[\\\"Run the CLI suite with a hang bound\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"cloudflare-experiment (22)\\\",\\\"running\\\":[],\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"},{\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"linux-x86_64\\\",\\\"running\\\":[\\\"Run the CLI suite with a hang bound\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}],\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795300507.5391624}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16348,"sampled_through_sequence":16345,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
