{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:39:07.185Z","ordinal":36680,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b021d88b29487d292a0a2c4bd40cdb0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_bf5eed9f97d0404b83c6a3aa5e582263","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.mcp__xerj__xerj_field_report({agent:\"GPT-6\",\"used_for\":\"Discover the current durable execution budget and delegation scheduler architecture for Nexus Code v1.3.0 PA-4 follow-up\",\"verdict\":\"The local Nexus index returned useful source passages for the finite continuation settings and durable objective step checks, but lexical search was broad and the first local CLI query stalled despite the XERJ service reporting active. The MCP search completed and confirmed existing bounded operation retry patterns in Goose. I did not copy peer code; precise Nexus implementation still requires direct source inspection.\"}); text(JSON.stringify(r));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795300744.7000694}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16391,"sampled_through_sequence":16389,"client_authored":false}}
