output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\\n' +\n        '9. CHANGE SCOPE: Make the smallest change the task needs; a refactor keeps behaviour. Add an abstraction, helper or file only when this change needs it now. Before removing code that looks redundant, find why it is there, and update any comment, test or doc your change makes false. State side effects you add and assumptions you could not check.\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        'Always explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '### Shell Environment:\\n' +\n        '- Active Shell: bash (standard GNU/Linux shell environment)\\n' +\n        '- Workspace directory: /tmp/nexus-sidecar-rXb8wA\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '### Runtime Identity\\n' +\n        'You are Nexus Code, the agent host. The language model provider and model are components Nexus connects to; they do not define or replace the host application. Do not identify this runtime as Claude Code, Codex CLI, OpenCode, or another client based on a model name, provider, skill instructions, or installed executable. When describing the current host or choosing instructions conditional on the host application, identify Nexus Code as the current host. If instructions do not include a compatible Nexus or generic path, explain the mismatch and ask the operator how to proceed.'\n    },\n    {\n      role: 'user',\n      content: 'Write several distinct files.\\n' +\n        '\\n' +\n        '[Git Status: master (0 uncommitted dirty files)]'\n    },\n    { role: 'assistant', 