{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T22:57:43.443Z","ordinal":37413,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b0221dc1dd487d284ce053410f5ff86","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2d9103be54bc4edc9886371a6faa9a9b","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget/docs/USER_MANUAL.md\\n@@\\n `--max-steps` (default 30) is a segment: at each segment boundary the turn writes a durable checkpoint and continues\\n-on its own. The objective has a finite default ceiling of 500 total steps and each invocation has a 480-minute ceiling.\\n-Operator overrides are bounded at 5,000 steps and 4,320 minutes. A turn also stops on completion, cancellation, demonstrated lack\\n+on its own. The objective has a finite default ceiling of 500 total steps and each invocation has a 480-minute ceiling.\\n+It also admits at most 1,000 tool dispatches for the objective by default. Set `--max-tool-invocations` or\\n+`NEXUS_MAX_TOOL_INVOCATIONS` to choose a different ceiling from 1 through 10,000. Operator overrides are bounded at\\n+5,000 steps and 4,320 minutes. A turn also stops on completion, cancellation, demonstrated lack\\n@@\\n-transient failures are spaced with backoff instead of being treated as loops. `--no-continuation` restores the\\n-single-segment turn. The objective ledger records the original request and open requirements; it survives compaction, follow-ups (\\\"continue\\\") and `/resume`; the total-step budget is shared with in-turn delegated\\n-helpers. The time limit currently applies to each active invocation and is not accumulated across process restarts.\\n+transient failures are spaced with backoff instead of being treated as loops. `--no-continuation` restores the\\n+single-segment turn but leaves the tool-dispatch ceiling active. The objective ledger records the original request and\\n+open requirements; it survives compaction, follow-ups (\\\"continue\\\") and `/resume`. The first tool-dispatch ceiling is\\n+saved with the objective; later runs can lower it, but cannot raise it for that objective. Older task records show the\\n+dispatch count as a lower bound because their earlier tool history was not recorded. The time limit currently applies\\n+to each active invocation and is not accumulated across process restarts.\\n@@\\n-A single model response may request at most 16 tool calls. A larger batch is rejected in full before any of its calls\\n-run, and Nexus reports the rejection in the next model context. This bounds tool fan-out from one response; it does\\n-not replace the objective-wide step budget.\\n+A single model response may request at most 16 tool calls. A larger batch is rejected in full before any of its calls\\n+run, and Nexus reports the rejection in the next model context. The objective-wide tool-dispatch ceiling also applies\\n+across responses: once exhausted, no further tool call is dispatched and the turn ends `LIMIT_REACHED` / `NOT_ESTABLISHED`.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795301852.1188035}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16715,"sampled_through_sequence":16713,"client_authored":false}}
