ool invocation admissions are bounded and legacy counts remain explicitly incomplete\", () => {\n    const tracker = ExecutionTracker.fresh();\n    assert.equal(tracker.admitToolInvocations(5, 2), 2);\n    assert.equal(tracker.admitToolInvocations(1, 2), 0);\n    assert.equal(tracker.data.toolInvocations, 2);\n    assert.equal(tracker.data.toolInvocationHistoryComplete, true);\n\n    const restored = normalizeTracking({ version: 1, cumulativeSteps: 4 });\n    assert.equal(restored.toolInvocations, 0);\n    assert.equal(restored.toolInvocationHistoryComplete, false);\n    assert.equal(new ExecutionTracker(restored).admitToolInvocations(1, 1), 1);\n    assert.equal(restored.toolInvocationHistoryComplete, false, \"new counts remain a lower bound after a legacy upgrade\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"an unfinished single-request objective continued with 'continue' keeps its ledger; new work starts a new one\", () => {\n    const ledger = createLedger(\"Refactor the parser\");\n    ledger.outcome = { status: \"incomplete\", reason: \"stagnation\", remaining: [], at: \"x\" };\n    for (const p of [\"continue\", \"Continue.\", \"keep going\", \"please continue where you left off\", \"try again\", \"resume\"]) {\n      assert.equal(isContinuationPrompt(p), true, p);\n      assert.equal(isNewObjective(ledger, p), false, p);\n    }\n    for (const p of [\"continue with the README instead\", \"fix the lexer\", \"Now write docs for it\"]) {\n      assert.equal(isNewObjective(ledger, p), true, p);\n    }\n    ledger.outcome = { status: \"completed\", reason: \"done\", remaining: [], at: \"x\" };\n    assert.equal(isNewObjective(ledger, \"continue\"), true, \"a completed objective is never continued\");\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:1:# Power of Ten Remediation Implementation Specification\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:37:**Gap/evidence:** `DEFAULT_CONTINUATION` sets total steps and minutes to Infinity (`cli/src/types.ts:182-188`); `runTurnImpl` checks a local `currentStep` (`run_turn.ts:137-145,220-267`); `runSubagent` uses an unbounded `for (;;)` (`agent.ts:4440-4457`); resumed invocation recreates local counters while cumulative steps are observational only (`turn.ts:348-359`).\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:41:**Design / reuse:** Extend `ContinuationBudget` and existing durable objective/operation records with a task budget id, maximum total steps/tool invocations/inference submissions/elapsed time/tokens, per-tool deadline and delegation depth. Persist consumed counters before/after side effects with `withDurableSync`. Child agents inherit the parent’s remaining budget; provider retry consumes the same inference allowance. A resumed task cannot regain budget. Require explicit operator-authorized budget renewal after exhaustion.\ndocs/assurance/POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:53:**Migration / rollback:** New config defaults may shorten formerly unlimited runs; provide an explicit operator override with a hard documented maximum, not Infinity. Keep old records readable. Rollback must not turn persisted exhausted state into zero; older binaries should refuse unsupported budget schema versions. Residual risk: already-running external calls may finish after cancellation or have unknown outcomes.\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:348:### Long tasks: bounded automatic continuation\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:357:transient failures are spaced with backoff instead of being treated as loops. `--no-continuation` restores the\ndocs/USER_MANUAL.md:390:ignored and `nexus doctor` warns. They work with `--no-continuation`. A project `.env` can only lower them: the\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"a5fa1dca (HEAD -> v1/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget, origin/main) Merge pull request #684 from mikeholownych/v1/pa4-transient-contract-tests\n1efb8625 (origin/v1/pa4-transient-contract-tests, v1/pa4-transient-contract-tests) test(delegation): exercise transient contract boundaries\nf3dc49dc Merge pull request #682 from mikeholownych/v1/pa4-provider-neutral-batch\ncbe1ead7 (origin/v1/pa4-provider-neutral-batch, v1/pa4-provider-neutral-batch) test(batch): adopt leak guard\nca4061d3 test(batch): exercise minimal provider workflow\n M cli/src/config.ts\n M cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts\n M cli/src/core/objective.ts\n M cli/src/core/run_turn.ts\n M cli/src/core/turn.ts\n M cli/src/index.ts\n M cli/src/types.ts\n M cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts\n M cli/test/objective_continuation.test.ts\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795301928.8746552}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16729,"sampled_through_sequence":16726,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
