{"timestamp":"2026-11-21T23:03:47.261Z","ordinal":37739,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b0223492b3487d29ee6adaa97cd79ea","status":"completed","call_id":"call_071eb1dc5d544547ba379e5284419045","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/p10-02-pr-body.md <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Add a durable objective-scoped tool dispatch ceiling (default 1,000; maximum 10,000), independent of automatic continuation.\\n- Reserve and persist dispatches before calling the tool dispatcher; reject remaining calls when the budget is exhausted or the reservation cannot be persisted.\\n- Persist the initial ceiling with the objective. A resumed objective may lower, but cannot increase, its saved ceiling.\\n- Mark legacy tracking history incomplete so migrated counters are not presented as exact zeroes.\\n- Document the behavior and update the v1.3.0 Power of Ten ledger with the completed slice and remaining work.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` — passed.\\n- `node --import tsx --test --test-name-pattern='tool invocation|burst of distinct writes|legacy objective continuation counts' test/execution_tracking.test.ts test/objective_continuation.test.ts` — 4 passed, 0 failed.\\n- Rust core rebuilt locally after rebasing on v1.2.2 to keep the fixture binary version aligned.\\n- Existing `main` hosted run `44956866625` passed before this PR; this PR still requires its own exact-head required checks.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- Reused Nexus's `ExecutionTracker`, objective continuation record, and `runTurnImpl` persistence/dispatch path; no second budget or scheduler subsystem was introduced.\\n- XERJ was consulted before implementation. The indexed Nexus passages confirmed the existing finite continuation and tracking architecture. A Goose reference query returned only a generic retry abstraction, so no peer code was copied. The local CLI query stalled; the MCP XERJ query completed. No provider code or provider-specific behavior was added.\\n\\n## Scope and limitations\\n\\n- This slice accounts direct agent turn dispatches. It does not yet share the counter with `runSubagent`, provider retries, inference submissions, token usage, cumulative elapsed time, or per-tool deadlines.\\n- Legacy objectives retain an explicitly incomplete prior count; reconciliation of historical dispatches is not available.\\n- Independent review remains pending. This PR must not be treated as completing the broader v1.3.0 delegation/orchestration assignment.\\nEOF\\ngh pr create --title \\\"feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches\\\" --body-file /tmp/p10-02-pr-body.md\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":2000});\ntext(JSON.stringify(r));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795302217.1712685}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":16862,"sampled_through_sequence":16859,"client_authored":false}}
