{"timestamp":"2026-11-22T02:34:45.694Z","ordinal":42327,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","response_id":"resp_0393e1fe95dcae93016b0254bbd89887d2b299ac57dbd2bea4","usage":{"input_tokens":125158,"cached_input_tokens":124800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":501,"reasoning_output_tokens":422,"total_tokens":125659},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":131735623,"cached_input_tokens":131079680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":155429,"reasoning_output_tokens":65090,"total_tokens":131891052},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":911420501,"cached_input_tokens":903817088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1295836,"reasoning_output_tokens":584634,"total_tokens":912716337}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-22T02:34:47.078Z","ordinal":42328,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dc2a66f9-e788-418c-86f1-12a2b59a2989","process_id":"92938","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 689 --json title,body --jq '{title,body}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 689 --json title,body --jq '{title,body}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"## Summary\\n\\n- Add a durable objective-scoped tool dispatch ceiling (default 1,000; maximum 10,000), independent of automatic continuation.\\n- Reserve and persist dispatches before calling the tool dispatcher; reject remaining calls when the budget is exhausted or the reservation cannot be persisted.\\n- Persist the initial ceiling with the objective. A resumed objective may lower, but cannot increase, its saved ceiling.\\n- Direct turns and in-turn delegated children share the same counter. A child reserves and persists each dispatch before execution.\\n- Mark legacy tracking history incomplete so migrated counters are not presented as exact zeroes.\\n- Document the behavior and update the v1.3.0 Power of Ten ledger with the completed slice and remaining work.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` — passed.\\n- Delegated budget regressions in `code_evaluators.test.ts` — 3 passed, 0 failed (shared count, exhaustion before dispatch, persistence failure before dispatch).\\n- `execution_tracking.test.ts` — 22 passed, 0 failed, including `read_tool_output` observer classification.\\n- `objective_continuation.test.ts` focused budget cases — 2 passed, 0 failed (bounded default/configuration and no renewal on resume).\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\n- Exact-head hosted checks are running after the delegated-budget fix.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- Reused Nexus's `ExecutionTracker`, objective continuation record, and `runTurnImpl` persistence/dispatch path; no second budget or scheduler subsystem was introduced.\\n- XERJ was consulted before implementation. OpenCode's `packages/codemode/src/tool-runtime.ts:384-410` admits/counts tool calls before executing them; its tests cover the cap. I used that reserve-before-effect pattern and rejected its optional/unlimited default for Nexus. No peer code was copied. The XERJ field report was submitted through its no-cost fallback after GitHub rejected the report fork.\\n\\n## Scope and limitations\\n\\n- This cap covers direct agent turns and transient in-turn delegated child dispatches. Durable work units, provider recovery/retries, inference submissions, token usage, cumulative elapsed time, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation remain separate work.\\n- Legacy objectives retain an explicitly incomplete prior count; historical dispatches cannot be reconstructed.\\n- This is a single-maintainer repository. The owner has directed that lack of a second reviewer must not hold publication; required exact-head hosted checks remain the publication gate.\\n\",\"title\":\"feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":172652594}},"started_at_ms":1795314885904,"completed_at_ms":1795314887077}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-22T02:34:47.247Z","ordinal":42329,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a2011b-2a4f-7012-a826-6bf3b361df22","call_id":"call_53711baa9ea448b9af296627c4782df2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f198f0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.172800376,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":656,\"output\":\"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"## Summary\\\\n\\\\n- Add a durable objective-scoped tool dispatch ceiling (default 1,000; maximum 10,000), independent of automatic continuation.\\\\n- Reserve and persist dispatches before calling the tool dispatcher; reject remaining calls when the budget is exhausted or the reservation cannot be persisted.\\\\n- Persist the initial ceiling with the objective. A resumed objective may lower, but cannot increase, its saved ceiling.\\\\n- Direct turns and in-turn delegated children share the same counter. A child reserves and persists each dispatch before execution.\\\\n- Mark legacy tracking history incomplete so migrated counters are not presented as exact zeroes.\\\\n- Document the behavior and update the v1.3.0 Power of Ten ledger with the completed slice and remaining work.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\n- `npm --prefix cli run build` — passed.\\\\n- Delegated budget regressions in `code_evaluators.test.ts` — 3 passed, 0 failed (shared count, exhaustion before dispatch, persistence failure before dispatch).\\\\n- `execution_tracking.test.ts` — 22 passed, 0 failed, including `read_tool_output` observer classification.\\\\n- `objective_continuation.test.ts` focused budget cases — 2 passed, 0 failed (bounded default/configuration and no renewal on resume).\\\\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\\\\n- Exact-head hosted checks are running after the delegated-budget fix.\\\\n\\\\n## Reference coding\\\\n\\\\n- Reused Nexus's `ExecutionTracker`, objective continuation record, and `runTurnImpl` persistence/dispatch path; no second budget or scheduler subsystem was introduced.\\\\n- XERJ was consulted before implementation. OpenCode's `packages/codemode/src/tool-runtime.ts:384-410` admits/counts tool calls before executing them; its tests cover the cap. I used that reserve-before-effect pattern and rejected its optional/unlimited default for Nexus. No peer code was copied. The XERJ field report was submitted through its no-cost fallback after GitHub rejected the report fork.\\\\n\\\\n## Scope and limitations\\\\n\\\\n- This cap covers direct agent turns and transient in-turn delegated child dispatches. Durable work units, provider recovery/retries, inference submissions, token usage, cumulative elapsed time, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation remain separate work.\\\\n- Legacy objectives retain an explicitly incomplete prior count; historical dispatches cannot be reconstructed.\\\\n- This is a single-maintainer repository. The owner has directed that lack of a second reviewer must not hold publication; required exact-head hosted checks remain the publication gate.\\\\n\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches\\\"}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795314887.247647}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":18790,"sampled_through_sequence":18787,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
