{"timestamp":"2026-11-22T02:35:05.235Z","ordinal":42333,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0393e1fe95dcae93016b0254ce3bc087d2aa13297c51b1f335","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a311d9ab810246719c4d9a7d6e562f18","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create --base release/v1.3.0 --head v1/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget --title 'feat(budgets): cap objective tool dispatches' --body-file - <<'EOF'\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Forward-port the objective-scoped tool invocation ceiling to `release/v1.3.0` after the same slice was merged to `main` in #689 (`745ec826`).\\n- Reserve and persist dispatches before calling the tool dispatcher; reject remaining calls when the budget is exhausted or reservation persistence fails.\\n- Persist the initial ceiling with the objective. A resumed objective may lower, but cannot increase, its saved ceiling.\\n- Direct turns and in-turn delegated children share the same counter.\\n- Mark legacy tracking history incomplete so migrated counters are not presented as exact zeroes.\\n- Document the behavior and update the v1.3.0 Power of Ten ledger.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- The same change set passed hosted `test-matrix (22)`, `test-matrix (24)`, and `linux-x86_64` for main head `8fb613a4` (run 44974336570).\\n- Release-branch exact-head CI is pending and is the merge gate for this PR.\\n- Local `git diff --check origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD` — passed.\\n- The earlier implementation build and focused budget regression tests passed before this forward-port; no local tests were started during this qualification because another local test process is running.\\n\\n## Reference coding\\n\\n- Reused Nexus's `ExecutionTracker`, objective continuation record, and `runTurnImpl` persistence/dispatch path; no second budget or scheduler subsystem was introduced.\\n- XERJ was consulted before implementation. OpenCode's `packages/codemode/src/tool-runtime.ts:384-410` admits/counts tool calls before executing them; its tests cover the cap. I used that reserve-before-effect pattern and rejected its optional/unlimited default for Nexus. No peer code was copied. The XERJ field report was submitted through its no-cost fallback after GitHub rejected the report fork.\\n\\n## Scope and limitations\\n\\n- This cap covers direct agent turns and transient in-turn delegated child dispatches. Durable work units, provider recovery/retries, inference submissions, token usage, cumulative elapsed time, per-tool deadlines, and process-crash reconciliation remain separate work.\\n- Legacy objectives retain an explicitly incomplete prior count; historical dispatches cannot be reconstructed.\\n- This is a single-maintainer repository. The owner has directed that lack of a second reviewer must not hold publication; required exact-head hosted checks remain the publication gate.\\nEOF\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10-02-tool-invocation-budget\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:700});text(JSON.stringify(r));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a2003f-4e12-7811-a5cb-72eb7d9f7819","create_time":1795314894.2353785}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":18792,"sampled_through_sequence":18790,"client_authored":false}}
